CHECKSUM.sha256 -- SHA-256 of every tracked file in this repository.
Generated : 2026-09-29; regenerated 2026-10-01 after the N=800 result and the
            certificate status sections landed, and after the three gates were
            made clone-portable (OMEGA_CORE_CERTIFICATE.md 6.1/6.6,
            PROVENANCE.txt 6.9).
            Regenerated 2026-10-02 after the consistency audit: README 4.1,
            REPO_STRUCTURE.md (inventory + not-produced table), WORKING_PAPER
            supplementary material, GW_STATUS_2026-09-26.md section 10
            (operational record 30 Sep - 1 Oct 2026). No file bytes other
            than documentation were altered.
            Regenerated again 2026-10-02 when Track C landed: OMEGATrackC.lean,
            track_c_make_smt.py, track_c_side_conditions.smt2 and the two
            evidence logs (track_c_smt_z3.log, track_c_lean_verify.log) were
            added, taking the list from 106 to 111 entries, and README 4.1,
            REPO_STRUCTURE.md, WORKING_PAPER.md, CITATION.cff and
            GW_STATUS_2026-09-26.md section 10 were rewritten from "no proof
            assistant has been run" to the measured tool status.
            Regenerated again 2026-10-02 after the certificate completeness
            pass: OMEGA_CORE_CERTIFICATE.md (header and scope now cover both
            certified targets, the two source-package SHA-256 values are
            reconciled, section 4.3 rewritten from the final telemetry, the
            three-phase N=800 run history and the D:\gw_ckpt timing
            corroboration added, new section 6.7 for Track C, reproduction
            cautions in section 8), THIRD_PARTY_SOURCES.md (size/SHA/use of
            the edited source package, scope statement) and PROVENANCE.txt
            (residual 6.10 and the updated tool status). No code, log, JSON
            or result file was altered by that pass.
            Regenerated again later on 2026-10-02 after the source-hash gate
            was made honest about the 2026-09-30 edit of the vendored source:
            gw_even_vs_src.py and gw_opt_a_diff.py now pin BOTH copies of
            source_arb_ldlt_certify.py (verbatim b7fee730... at git b76be0d,
            shipped 33617ce6... since commit bfa40dc) and fail on any third
            value, and gw_even_vs_src_100_200_rerun_20261002.log was added as
            the rerun evidence (exit 0, same delta / delta_rel / V1 verdict as
            the 2026-09-29 log, only wall-clock times differ).  THIRD_PARTY_
            SOURCES.md, PROVENANCE.txt 6.10, GW_STATUS 7g.3 and section 10, and
            certificate 6.1 record the same thing.  Entries 111 -> 112; two
            .py gate scripts changed, no result file and no pre-existing log
            was edited.
            The manifest excludes itself by construction.
Paths are REPOSITORY-RELATIVE and use forward slashes. The previous
version of this file recorded absolute Windows paths (C:\Users\...),
which leaked a local username into a public repository; that is fixed
here. File contents are unchanged by that edit.
The previous version was also UTF-16 encoded (PowerShell Out-File default),
which is why git has always reported this file as "Bin ..." in --stat: a
UTF-16 byte stream puts a NUL in every other byte and git then treats the
diff as binary. That occurred in commits de68a32 and 8ec0745, before this
rewrite. This version is UTF-8 / LF / pure ASCII, so from the next change
onward the manifest will diff as text.
