            Regenerated 2026-10-04 after the F0 anti-circularity audit: five
            Track C hashes above changed (OMEGATrackC.lean, track_c_make_smt.py,
            track_c_side_conditions.smt2, track_c_lean_verify.log,
            track_c_smt_z3.log) plus OMEGA_CORE_CERTIFICATE.md section 6.7.
            Four false docstrings were corrected and implied_constant_gt_81
            (strict, held only by the binary64 rounding of rhoStar) was replaced
            by implied_constant_ge_81 (non-strict). No numeric literal changed.
            See F0_REPORT.md at the workspace root.

            Regenerated 2026-10-04 after the F1 numeric-canon and pipeline
            audit. Four tracked sources changed:
              gw_verify_results.py      unguarded fixture read and row index
                                        replaced by verdicts; missing required
                                        keys recorded and skipped instead of
                                        raising KeyError; sha256 test now
                                        matches its own message and requires
                                        64 HEX characters (64 'z's passed
                                        before).  Fault injection: 14/14.
              gw_verify_production.py   deep invariants enforced (dimension =
                                        2N+1, 64-hex sha256, bound re-derived
                                        from bound_detail, pivot sign) on
                                        fixtures and production; docstring
                                        synced.  Fault injection: 14/14.
              gw_final_gate.py          one gate condition replaced by two --
                                        G1 some side resolves below lambda_min
                                        and G2 the rejected mpmath side is
                                        accounted for by the lerchphi gap --
                                        plus a (c, N) provenance guard and a
                                        resolution-aware VERDICT.
              gw_mont_pipeline_check.py anchored to its own directory so it no
                                        longer reports a false K1-K6 alarm when
                                        invoked from another cwd.
            gw_final_gate_run.log is added as the F1 proof artifact of a full
            PASS run (G1 and G2 both satisfied).  The gate threshold lambda_min
            and every certified numeric literal are unchanged.  See
            F1_REPORT.md at the workspace root.
            Regenerated 2026-10-04 after the F1 blind-spot re-review (F1-R1..R4):
            three ship-inventory rows in OMEGA_CORE_CERTIFICATE.md went stale
            the moment the F1 gates above were edited, which the F1 pass itself
            had not caught.  Section 6.1 now carries the post-F1 bytes of
            gw_verify_results.py and gw_verify_production.py plus a provenance
            bullet recording what changed and the superseded hashes; section
            6.6 keeps the 2026-10-01 bytes of gw_verify_production.py on
            purpose and now says so; section 6.2 discloses that its three rows
            are the N=400 snapshot (expected not to match the working tree),
            that the working-tree run log is two appended runs, and that the
            "remains in this repository's git history" sentence is not
            verifiable from a copy without .git.  README section 7 dropped a
            silently ignored argument from the gw_verify_results.py
            invocation, which contradicted the override note in section 8, and
            REPO_STRUCTURE.md records that gw_final_gate.py is provenance-
            locked to c=100, N=400.  Three documentation files changed; no
            gate, log, JSON or result file was touched in this pass.

            Also 2026-10-04: the manifest itself was not clean.  It listed
            `Framework.md`, which does not exist anywhere under the repository,
            and it did not list the file that does exist under its long title
            ("Rigorous Ball Arithmetic and Bandwidth-Calibrated Spectral Analysis
            of the Guinand-Weil Operator Framework.md", 11163 bytes), so a
            verifier walking the tree would have reported one dead row and one
            uncovered file.  Both are fixed here: the dead row is dropped and
            the present file is hashed.  Whether the two names are a rename
            cannot be established from a copy with no `.git`, so no rename is
            claimed.  This pass also confirms that `__pycache__/` is excluded by
            this manifest, consistently with the repository's own .gitignore.

            Also 2026-10-04, from widening that same scan past the certificate:
            PROVENANCE.txt reported 10 rows that no longer resolve, 8 of them
            historical by design (it is a dated snapshot and says so) and 2 of
            them F1's own.  A section 8 was ADDED to PROVENANCE.txt listing all
            ten with their causes, and the section 1 claim that
            gw_mont_pipeline_check.py was "intentionally LEFT UNCHANGED" is
            retracted in place rather than struck.  Sections 1-5 of
            PROVENANCE.txt were not edited.  The same pass corrected F1-D: the
            N=400 lambda_min is recorded in three places that agree (run log
            line 51 at 25 sf, PROVENANCE 6.2 and the certificate section 4 JSON
            block at 30 sf) but the result FILE was overwritten by the N=800 run
            and no 1971-byte JSON survives anywhere, so it is "recorded but not
            machine-gated" rather than "log-recorded only".  Skill.md's
            lambda_min status line now says that.  No gate, log, JSON or result
            file was touched by this pass either.

Regenerated 2026-10-05 after F2-7: gw_verify_production.py hardened

